# Vaani Docker and Deployment

Vaani uses Docker for containerization and GitHub Actions for CI/CD. The deployment process is fully automated for both staging and production environments.

## Docker Configuration

### Backend Services

Each backend service has its own Dockerfile:

- [API Gateway](mdc:backend/services/api-gateway/Dockerfile)
- [Media Service](mdc:backend/services/media-service/Dockerfile)
- [Bulbul Adapter](mdc:backend/services/bulbul-adapter/Dockerfile)
- [Orpheus Inference](mdc:backend/services/orpheus-inference/Dockerfile)

For local development, all services are orchestrated using [docker-compose.yml](mdc:backend/infra/docker/docker-compose.yml).

### Frontend Web

The Flutter web application is containerized using [Dockerfile](mdc:frontend/Dockerfile) which:
1. Builds the Flutter web app
2. Serves it using Nginx

## Deployment Process

### GitHub Actions Workflows

- [ci-go.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/ci-go.yml) - Tests and lints Go code on PRs
- [ci-flutter.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/ci-flutter.yml) - Tests and builds Flutter web on PRs
- [deploy-staging.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml) - Deploys to staging on merge to main
- [release.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/release.yml) - Deploys to production on release tags

### Docker Registry

Docker images are pushed to GitHub Container Registry (ghcr.io) with tags:
- `staging` for staging environment
- Version number (e.g., `v1.0.0`) and `latest` for production

### Infrastructure as Code

Terraform is used to manage infrastructure. The Terraform configurations are stored in `backend/infra/terraform/` and use workspaces for different environments:
- `staging` for staging environment
- `prod` for production environment

### Web Deployment

The web application is deployed to Firebase Hosting:
- Staging: on merge to main
- Production: on release tags

### Mobile App Deployment

Mobile apps (Android AAB, iOS IPA) are built on release tags and uploaded as build artifacts, ready for distribution to:
- Play Store internal track
- TestFlight beta
